    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "The repeated fall/teleport loop came from a climb target below Arthur's live root while the entry impulse still forced him upward. The old floor check also used an impossible root-height threshold, the top-out test treated a foot probe as the head, and weak aggregate support allowed empty-space anchors. Source now solves from the live root and contact plane, requires upper and lower support, blocks underground/unsupported movement before writing coordinates, and hands only a proved landing to vanilla climb. Unsafe angled alignment now releases instead of pretending it is fitted. The focused contract passes 67 guards and rejects 27 regressions. This has not been built or installed, so Lexer-Lux/Lexeditor#261 stays actionable.",
